{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged at ff6132ece049e9e65245ac8ddb7a733c4bb48fdb: the gs command line at cmd/gs. The private citation guard is gone from here; supersedeCommand and batchCommand now carry --cited-ok through Act.CitedOK to the shared boundary in internal/app, and gs batch keeps its whole-file pre-flight calling the same exported guard so a batch that cannot land cleanly still lands nothing.\n\nIt rests on 4eeb3acf, the live non-stale artifact at this path whose commit is in main.\n\nDeliberately NOT retiring 24d800c0, the other live shipped artifact at this path, and recording why rather than leaving it as an omission. Measured before deciding: 24d800c0 has 81 transitive dependents, and retiring it would stale three currently-clean artifacts — 663a2275, 0044d580 and d98404cc — and make two open review requests unmergeable, b94df9d4 for the projection notes at 5a2a32c9 and dca96364 for the dead Stream rows at a4763853. Both heads are reviewed work waiting on a verdict. Leaving cmd/gs temporarily carrying two shipped artifacts is a smaller harm than invalidating two in-flight heads, and it is reversible: I will retire 24d800c0 once those merge. This is the tradeoff eae77d2c exists to remove — under a temporal reading, retiring it could not reach back into verdicts signed before the retirement, and there would be nothing to defer.","body":{"commit":"ff6132ece049e9e65245ac8ddb7a733c4bb48fdb","path":"cmd/gs"}}